It is a cold evening.
The wind is strong, and my jacket is too thin.
I am very cold.
I walk quickly into a supermarket.
It is wonderfully warm here.
I am calling my family in Mexico tonight.
It is an important call for me.
I buy a pastry and a tea.
I find a box with tea.
I also choose a Danish pastry.
I walk over to a register.
A young man works there.
He scans my tea and my pastry.
"That will be thirty-eight kroner," he says.
I pay with my card.
"Your receipt?" he asks.
"No thank you," I reply.
I take my things from the counter.
Now I am ready.
I walk out into the cold again.
